(6) The following expenses may be deducted without regard to the deductible: 
— expenses for the elimination of disaster damage, in particular flood, landslide, mudslide and avalanche damage; 
— costs of external vocational training under subsection (8); 
— additional expenses of the taxpayer for persons for whom increased family allowance is granted pursuant to Section 8(4) of the Family Burden Equalisation Act 1967; 
— expenses within the meaning of Section 35 which are claimed in lieu of the flat-rate amounts (Section 35(5)).

